{"kind":"assert","text":"Hugh's decisions on the act environment note, for request `98f450a1`.\n\nOn 14 November 2026 Hugh decided the seven items of section 17 of `notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md`, with the words \"yes - agreed\". Draft 4 of the note records the decisions, at commit `f760e3714b` on branch `planner/act-environment-20261114`. The decisions answer items 2 and 3 of \"What the planner does\" in the request.\n\n1. Decision A, a subject's admission as `observed` or `current`: yes. The environment gives no step a new basis by itself. Step A is the last step. Its own design names the carrier and takes the kernel ruling.\n2. The authorization rule in place of D12 rule 3: yes. The first build has only the default deadline.\n3. The change of D12 rule 5: yes. C4 takes the rule from its first build.\n4. The export of the body judgment from `packages/derive`: yes, on the condition that `judgeAct` gives identical answers on the replay corpus.\n5. One owner key for each step: yes.\n6. The method `explore` on `ScopeApi`: held. Step E2 is the MCP tool on a replica in the agent host, and it needs C2. A review after step E3 takes the method up again.\n7. The third symbolic name, `{ entry }`: yes, with the coarse rule of section 5.4.\n\nFour things remain for the planner: the review and the landing of the note, the ruling under `docs/kernel.md` sections 7 and 7.1 for the export of step E1, Hugh's ratification of the note, and one child request for each build step of section 13.\n\nThis statement records Hugh's words. It is not the ruling.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}